{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "studzee-backend-api-collection",
    "name": "Studzee Backend API",
    "description": "Backend service for content delivery and notifications. Covers health checks, public content, PDF listing, device registration for push, the Clerk webhook, and the admin surface for documents, notifications, email and users.\n\nThe notification service was merged into this backend, so the endpoints that used to sit behind /noti/api are now served here under /notifications, /admin and /webhooks.\n\nSETUP\n\n1. Set baseUrl if the API is not on http://localhost:4000.\n2. For authenticated and admin routes, set clerkToken. Use a Clerk session JWT, or for local work paste the DEV_TOKEN value from BACKEND/.env, which grants admin rights and is ignored outside NODE_ENV=development.\n3. Run Get Paginated Content once. It saves the first document id into the documentId variable, so every request that needs an id works without copying values by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health Check",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Welcome",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": [""]
            },
            "description": "Root route. Returns the service name and a map of the main endpoints, useful for confirming which build is deployed."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Liveness Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/liveness",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health", "liveness"]
            },
            "description": "Checks if the application is running."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Healthcheck (Production)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthcheck",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["healthcheck"]
            },
            "description": "Simple health check endpoint for Render or other hosting platforms. This is the URL the heartbeat job pings."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/readiness",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health", "readiness"]
            },
            "description": "Checks every backing store the service needs: MongoDB for content, Postgres for users and notifications, and Redis for caching.\n\nEach check issues a real round trip rather than reading a driver connection flag, so it cannot report healthy while a store has stopped answering. Probes run in parallel with a 2 second timeout each.\n\nReturns 200 with every check ok, or 503 naming the store that failed."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Content",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List Topics",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/content/topics",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["content", "topics"]
            },
            "description": "The fixed topic registry in display order. Public. Use these keys for filtering and for labelling sections."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"returns the registry\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200)",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.be.an(\"array\")",
                  "})"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Today's Content",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/content/today",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["content", "today"]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve documents created during the current IST day, which runs from 18:30 UTC to 18:30 UTC."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Paginated Content",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/content?page=1&limit=20&topic=machine-learning",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["content"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "topic",
                  "value": "machine-learning",
                  "description": "Optional registry key filter. Unknown keys answer 400."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a paginated list of documents, optionally scoped to one topic from the fixed registry. Items carry their topic key so clients can group a page locally."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Saves the first document id into the documentId collection variable,",
                  "// so the requests that need an id work without copying values by hand.",
                  "const body = pm.response.json()",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"returns a paginated list\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200)",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"data\")",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"meta\")",
                  "})",
                  "",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"documentId\", body.data[0]._id)",
                  "    console.log(\"documentId set to \" + body.data[0]._id)",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log(\"no documents returned, run npm run seed first\")",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Document by ID",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/content/:id",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["content", ":id"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{documentId}}",
                  "description": "Taken from the documentId collection variable, which Get Paginated Content sets for you."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a complete document by its ID. Requires authentication. Documents carrying an unlockPoints cost answer 403 with code CONTENT_LOCKED when the caller has fewer points."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "PDFs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List All PDFs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/pdfs?page=1&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["pdfs"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a paginated list of documents with uploaded PDFs, flattened to one entry per PDF."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Notifications",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Device",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"learner@example.com\",\n  \"expoToken\": \"ExponentPushToken[xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notifications/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["notifications", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register the caller's device for push notifications, or attach another device token to an existing registration. The Clerk identity comes from the bearer token, never from the body. Tokens are deduplicated, so re-registering the same device does not create a second entry.\n\nReplaces POST /noti/api/register from the old notification service.\n\nRate limit: 10 requests per minute."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Progress",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get My Progress",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{clerkToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/progress/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["progress", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Points, level and next level, streaks, active days, earned badges plus the full catalog with awarded flags, and recent attempts. Requires authentication."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"returns progress\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200)",
                  "    const d = pm.response.json().data",
                  "    pm.expect(d).to.have.property(\"points\")",
                  "    pm.expect(d).to.have.property(\"badges\")",
                  "})"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit Quiz Attempt",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{clerkToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"contentId\": \"{{documentId}}\",\n  \"responses\": {\n    \"q1\": 0,\n    \"q2\": 1\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/progress/attempts",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["progress", "attempts"]
            },
            "description": "Grades a quiz server side against the stored answers (responses maps each quiz question key to the chosen option index), records the attempt, awards points as a delta over prior best for that content, and updates streaks and badges. 404 when the content has no quiz."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"grades the attempt\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200)",
                  "    const d = pm.response.json().data",
                  "    pm.expect(d).to.have.property(\"score\")",
                  "    pm.expect(d).to.have.property(\"totalPoints\")",
                  "})"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Webhooks",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Clerk Webhook",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "svix-id",
                "value": "msg_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
                "description": "Supplied by Clerk on every delivery"
              },
              {
                "key": "svix-timestamp",
                "value": "1700000000",
                "description": "Supplied by Clerk on every delivery"
              },
              {
                "key": "svix-signature",
                "value": "v1,xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
                "description": "Supplied by Clerk on every delivery"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"user.created\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"user_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\",\n    \"email_addresses\": [\n      { \"id\": \"idn_xxxxxxxx\", \"email_address\": \"learner@example.com\" }\n    ],\n    \"first_name\": \"Learner\",\n    \"last_name\": null,\n    \"username\": null\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webhooks/clerk",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["webhooks", "clerk"]
            },
            "description": "Receives Clerk events. Only user.created is acted on, which sends the welcome email.\n\nThis endpoint takes no user token. The svix signature is its only authentication, and the handler verifies the raw request bytes. A request sent from Postman without valid svix headers signed by CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET will correctly return 400. Use the Clerk dashboard's webhook tester for a real end to end check.\n\nThe endpoint always answers 2xx once the signature verifies, including when the welcome email fails, because a non 2xx makes Clerk redeliver and resend the email."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin - Documents",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Document",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"New Tutorial\",\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Introduction\",\n      \"content\": [\n        { \"type\": \"text\", \"value\": \"Opening paragraph.\" },\n        { \"type\": \"list\", \"items\": [\"First point\", \"Second point\"] }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Optional summary of the content\",\n  \"facts\": \"Optional interesting facts\",\n  \"quiz\": {\n    \"q1\": {\n      \"que\": \"Sample question?\",\n      \"ans\": \"Correct answer\",\n      \"options\": [\"Option 1\", \"Option 2\", \"Correct answer\", \"Option 4\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"key_notes\": {\n    \"note1\": \"Important point 1\",\n    \"note2\": \"Important point 2\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/documents",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "documents"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new document. Requires the admin role.\n\nNote that `content` is structured, either an array of sections or an object. It is not a plain string."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"document created\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201)",
                  "})",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json()",
                  "if (body.doc && body.doc._id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"documentId\", body.doc._id)",
                  "    console.log(\"documentId set to the new document \" + body.doc._id)",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Document",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Updated Tutorial Title\",\n  \"summary\": \"Updated summary text\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/documents/:id",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "documents", ":id"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{documentId}}",
                  "description": "Taken from the documentId collection variable, which Get Paginated Content sets for you."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Update an existing document. Requires the admin role.\n\nThe body is a partial document validated against the same schema as create, so any subset of the document fields is accepted and at least one field is required."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Document",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/documents/:id",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "documents", ":id"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{documentId}}",
                  "description": "Taken from the documentId collection variable, which Get Paginated Content sets for you."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Delete a document by its ID. Requires the admin role."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload Document Image",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Image file (JPG, PNG, or WebP, max 10MB)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/documents/:id/upload-image",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "documents", ":id", "upload-image"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{documentId}}",
                  "description": "Taken from the documentId collection variable, which Get Paginated Content sets for you."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Upload the cover image for a document. Replaces any existing image. Requires the admin role.\n\nIMPORTANT: in the Body tab, the form-data row named file is only a placeholder. You must click Select Files and choose an actual file, otherwise Postman sends nothing and the request fails with 400 No file uploaded. The field name must be file."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Upload Document PDF",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "PDF file (max 50MB)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/documents/:id/upload-pdf",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "documents", ":id", "upload-pdf"],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{documentId}}",
                  "description": "Taken from the documentId collection variable, which Get Paginated Content sets for you."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Attach a PDF to a document. Documents hold an array of PDFs, so this appends rather than replaces. Requires the admin role.\n\nIMPORTANT: in the Body tab, click Select Files on the form-data row named file and choose a real PDF. A row with no file attached sends nothing and fails with 400 No file uploaded. The field name must be file."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin - Notifications",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send Push Notification (All Users)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"New notes published\",\n  \"message\": \"System Design chapter 4 is now available.\",\n  \"imageUrl\": \"https://lammfakgegmrkxdkwukd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/images/banner.png\",\n  \"sendToAll\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/notifications/send",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "notifications", "send"]
            },
            "description": "Broadcast a push notification to every registered device. Requires the admin role.\n\nMessages are chunked to the Expo limit of 100 per request, so a broadcast larger than that is split across several calls. Tokens Expo reports as DeviceNotRegistered are pruned immediately.\n\nReturns 200 when every message was accepted and 207 when the broadcast was only partially delivered, with sent, failed and prunedTokens counts in the body.\n\nReplaces POST /noti/api/admin/notification/send.\n\nRate limit: 20 requests per minute."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Send Push Notification (Named Users)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Your quiz result\",\n  \"message\": \"You scored 8 out of 10.\",\n  \"sendToAll\": false,\n  \"emails\": [\"learner@example.com\"]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/notifications/send",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "notifications", "send"]
            },
            "description": "Send to the devices belonging to a named set of users. `emails` is required and must be non empty whenever `sendToAll` is false, which the schema enforces. Returns 404 when none of the named users have a registered device."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Sent Notifications",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/notifications?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=createdAt&order=desc",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "notifications"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sortBy",
                  "value": "createdAt",
                  "description": "One of createdAt, status, sentBy. Anything else falls back to createdAt."
                },
                {
                  "key": "order",
                  "value": "desc",
                  "description": "asc or desc"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Paginated history of sent notifications. Requires the admin role.\n\nReplaces GET /noti/api/admin/notifications.\n\nRate limit: 30 requests per minute."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin - Email",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send Email",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{clerkToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"emails\": [\"learner@example.com\"],\n  \"subject\": \"New notes are available\",\n  \"title\": \"New notes are available\",\n  \"body\": \"<p>Chapter 4 of System Design is published.</p>\",\n  \"footer\": \"This is an automated email from Studzee.\",\n  \"pdfUrls\": [\n    \"https://lammfakgegmrkxdkwukd.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/pdfs/system-design.pdf\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/emails/send",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "emails", "send"]
            },
            "description": "Send a transactional email. Requires the admin role.\n\n`body` is an HTML fragment composed by the caller and dropped into the shared template. Recipients are sent as bcc, so one broadcast does not disclose the list to everyone on it.\n\nAttachments are fetched by the mail transport at send time, so every entry in `pdfUrls` must be https on a host listed in EMAIL_ATTACHMENT_HOSTS, with at most 10 per message. Anything else returns a failure without sending.\n\nReturns 502 when the transport rejects the message. Replaces POST /noti/api/admin/email/send.\n\nRate limit: 10 requests per minute."
